Explanation:

1. The gradient vector $nabla f(P)$ acts as the normal vector $bold(n)$ to the level surface at point $P(1, -1, 2)$.
Given $nabla f(P) = chevron.l 2, 5, -3 chevron.r$, the normal is $bold(n) = chevron.l 2, 5, -3 chevron.r$.
2. The equation of the plane through $P(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ with normal $bold(n) = chevron.l A, B, C chevron.r$ is:
$ A(x - x_0) + B(y - y_0) + C(z - z_0) = 0 $
3. Substituting the values:
$ 2(x - 1) + 5(y - (-1)) - 3(z - 2) = 0 $
$ 2x - 2 + 5y + 5 - 3z + 6 = 0 $
$ 2x + 5y - 3z = -9 $.
